{"type":"message","id":"4c26ba70","parentId":"72b1fb9f","timestamp":"2026-10-29T02:35:38.072Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_02_pqDfVmyntzIrlEdyo6NY0437","toolName":"web_fetch","content":[{"type":"text","text":"View Page Source Tool — Free Online HTML Source Code Viewer | IndexCraft\nHome\nAbout\nWeb Tools\nContact\nInstant · Free · No signup needed\n# View Page Source — Online HTML Source Code Viewer\nPaste any public URL and get its raw, line-numbered HTML source instantly — the same markup search engines and AI crawlers read. Highlight a keyword, copy the full source, or download it as a .txt file in one click.\n🔗 Any Public URL\n📄 Raw HTML Source\n🏷️ Key Meta Tag Extraction\n🔍 Keyword Highlight\n📋 One-Click Copy\n⬇️ Download as .TXT\nTL;DR\nView Page Source is a free online tool that fetches and displays the raw HTML code of any public webpage — the exact markup a server sends, before JavaScript changes anything — directly in your browser tab. Enter a URL, get a line-numbered source view instantly, then copy it or download it as a plain .txt file. No installation and no account required.\nWebpage URL\nHighlight Keyword (optional)\nView Source\nClear\nConnecting…\n0%\nPreparing request…\n# Key Meta Tags Detected\nAuto-extracted straight from the fetched source — a quick way to sanity-check title length, canonical tags and indexability without scrolling the raw HTML.\n# Raw HTML Source\nCopy Source\nDownload TXT\nOpen Page\n# Page Source vs. Rendered DOM\nPage Source\nThe raw HTML file exactly as the server sent it, before any JavaScript runs. This is what this tool shows, and it's the baseline markup most crawlers — including search engines and AI answer engines — read first.\nRendered DOM\nThe live page structure after JavaScript has finished adding, editing, or removing elements — what you see in your browser's DevTools \"Elements\" panel. On JavaScript-heavy sites this can differ significantly from the page source.\n# What This Tool Checks\nView Page Source fetches the target URL through IndexCraft's own server-side proxy — since browsers block a webpage from directly reading another site's HTML — then parses the result entirely in your browser.\n# 📄 Raw Source Fetch\nPulls the exact HTML a server returns for a given URL, before JavaScript execution.\n# 🏷️ Meta Tag Extraction\nPulls out title, meta description, canonical, meta robots and viewport tags automatically.\n# 📊 Quick Stats\nFile size, line count, character count, and counts of images, scripts and links.\n# 🔍 Keyword Highlight\nHighlights every occurrence of a keyword or tag name across the source view.\n# 📋 One-Click Copy\nCopies the complete, untruncated source to your clipboard.\n# ⬇️ Download as .TXT\nSaves the full source as a plain-text file named after the site's domain.\n# How to Use\nPaste a full URL (with https:// ) into the input above, optionally add a keyword to highlight, and click View Source . The tool fetches the page, extracts key meta tags, and renders a line-numbered source view. Use Copy Source or Download TXT to save the complete file.\n# When a URL Won't Load\nSome sites block automated/proxy requests, require login, sit behind a firewall, or serve different content to bots — in those cases the fetch will fail. As a manual fallback, most desktop browsers let you type view-source: followed by the URL directly into the address bar.\n# Frequently Asked Questions\nWhat does \"view page source\" actually mean?\nViewing page source means reading the raw HTML file a server sends before any JavaScript runs. It's the same markup search engine crawlers, AI crawlers and browsers start with, and it's different from the live DOM you see in DevTools after scripts finish rendering the page.\nWhy can't this tool read every website?\nBrowsers block a webpage from directly fetching another site's HTML for security reasons, known as the same-origin policy. This tool routes the request through IndexCraft's own server-side proxy to work around that. Some sites block automated requests, require a login, or return different content to bots, so a small number of URLs will fail to load.\nIs view-source the same as the rendered HTML in DevTools?\nNo. View-source shows the original HTML delivered by the server. DevTools' Elements panel shows the live DOM after JavaScript has added, removed or changed elements. For JavaScript-heavy sites, the two can look very different.\nDoes this tool store or upload the pages I view?\nNo. The fetched HTML is processed and rendered directly in your browser tab and isn't saved on IndexCraft's servers. Note that the request itself passes through IndexCraft's own server-side proxy to reach the target site, so it isn't a fully local, offline process.\nCan I use this to check if a page has noindex or a canonical tag?\nYes. The Key Meta Tags panel automatically pulls out the title tag, meta description, canonical URL, meta robots directive and viewport tag from the fetched source, so you can quickly spot a stray noindex or a missing canonical without scrolling through the raw HTML.\nWhy is the source only showing part of a very large page?\nTo keep the page fast and your browser responsive, the on-screen viewer displays the first few thousand lines. The Copy and Download TXT buttons always use the complete, untruncated source, so nothing is missing from what you copy or save.\n# Text Tools\n- Binary to Decimal\n- Remove Empty Lines\n- Remove Extra Whitespaces\n- Decimal to Hex\n- Reverse Text Generator\n# Image Tools\n- AVIF to PNG\n- Image to Base64\n- JPG to PNG Converter\n- PNG to JPG Converter\n- YouTube Thumbnail Downloader\n# Calculators & Converters\n- Pressure Converter\n- Weight Converter\n- Torque Converter\n- Sales Tax Calculator\n- Discount Calculator\n# Development Tools\n- View Page Source\n- LogCraft Log Analyser\n- Schema Markup Generator\n- NS Lookup\n- JSON Formatter / Validator\n© 2026 IndexCraft. All rights reserved. | About | Terms of Use | Privacy Policy\n\n## Links\n(no text) -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/\nHome -> https://theindexcraft.com/\nAbout -> https://theindexcraft.com/about\nWeb Tools -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/\nContact -> https://theindexcraft.com/contact\nOpen Page -> https://pagesource.wasmer.app/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpudding.cool%2F2024%2F11%2Fsitters-standers%2F#\nBinary to Decimal -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/text-analysis/binary-to-decimal\nRemove Empty Lines -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/text-analysis/remove-empty-and-duplicate-lines\nRemove Extra Whitespaces -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/text-analysis/remove-extra-whitespaces\nDecimal to Hex -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/text-analysis/decimal-to-hex\nReverse Text Generator -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/text-analysis/reverse-text-generator\nAVIF to PNG -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/image-editing-tools/avif-to-png\nImage to Base64 -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/image-editing-tools/image-to-base64\nJPG to PNG Converter -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/image-editing-tools/jpg-to-png-converter\nPNG to JPG Converter -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/image-editing-tools/png-to-jpg-converter\nYouTube Thumbnail Downloader -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/image-editing-tools/youtube-thumbnail-downloader\nPressure Converter -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/calculators-converters/pressure-converter\nWeight Converter -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/calculators-converters/weight-converter\nTorque Converter -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/calculators-converters/torque-converter\nSales Tax Calculator -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/calculators-converters/sales-tax-calculator\nDiscount Calculator -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/calculators-converters/discount-calculator\nView Page Source -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/developer-tools/view-page-source\nLogCraft Log Analyser -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/dev-tools/logcraft\nSchema Markup Generator -> https://tools.theindexcraft.com/seo-tools/sch